**Standard axes**: down migration = ordered deletes (runs→snapshots→labels→drop own tables→source), never drops shared `wallet_labels` ✓; all SQL parameterized via sqlc, generated file consistent ✓; `ctx` threaded end-to-end incl. explicit `ctx.Err()` in scan loop; 30s timeout + bounded retry + breaker + rate limit + SSRF allowlist (https-only, `rpc.ankr.com`) ✓; `Removed:true` logs rejected (reorg guard) ✓; publish entirely on `qtx` inside the service-managed tx, rollback-before-finish ordering preserved ✓; no `[:12]`-style slicing on attacker-controlled strings; fail-closed everywhere required (missing cursors, missing provider, malformed ts); no secrets logged in the new paths except finding 2's narrow vector; tests honest — additive only, `_test` DB via `testutil`, cursor state restored in cleanup, no skips/weakens. No `go test`/`go build` run — per mandate, orchestrator runs gates.

